# Tests ship with the change

When you change user-facing behaviour, update tests **in the same commit/PR** — not after production feedback.

## Definition of done

1. Implement the change
2. Update or add tests that exercise the **real interaction** (not only mocked shortcuts)
3. Run `npm run build` and `npm run test:e2e`
4. Update `docs/QA-TEST-PLAN.md` if coverage scope or test IDs change

## Playwright (`e2e/*.spec.ts`)

| Change type | Test expectation |
|-------------|------------------|
| New/changed UI flow | New or updated spec; click/type like a user |
| Copy, labels, classes | Update assertions (including `production-smoke.spec.ts` if user-visible) |
| External API (Places, etc.) | Mock the API in `e2e/helpers.ts`; assert UI outcome |
| Photo/upload/crop | Use file picker (`waitForEvent('filechooser')`) or label click — **do not** only inject `input.files` unless also covered by a click test |

## Avoid false confidence

- Mocked Supabase passing ≠ integration working
- `input.files` + `change` alone does **not** prove click-to-upload works
- Silent `catch` + empty results (e.g. Places returning `[]`) needs an error/warning assertion or a mocked failure test

## Still manual (document in QA-TEST-PLAN)

Real API keys, Netlify functions on prod, device camera/HEIC, live Supabase writes — note in manual smoke, don’t skip because e2e mocks exist.
